// T4: BoundNodes.cs, BoundTree.cs and the BoundMethodGroup/BoundBuiltinGroup/BoundVariantGroup records from BinderExpressions.cs.
//
// A bound node is a handle `(BoundKind << 32) | index` into the per-kind arena on `Ctx` (`bLiterals`,
// `bCalls`, …); -1 is C#'s `null`. `BExpr`, `BStmt` and `BPattern` (ctx.byn) share the one `BoundKind`, so
// any of them is a `BNode`. One struct per C# record, fields in C# order: `Node Syntax` is `TextSpan span`,
// a symbol is its T3 handle, `T[]` is a `List<T>`, and a base type computed from a symbol or a child
// (`BoundLocal`'s `Local.Type`) is a trailing `type` the constructor fills. `BoundExpr.Constant` lives in
// `Ctx.constants` and the facts C# reads from `Syntax` in `Ctx.syntaxFlags`, both keyed by the handle (Q537).
// Helper records that are not nodes (`BSwitchArm`, `BSwitchSection`, …) are stored inline in their parent.

import parser

public type BNode = i64

// ── Kinds ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Every concrete `BoundExpr`, `BoundStmt` and `BoundPattern` record of `BoundNodes.cs` in file order, then the
/// three group records of `BinderExpressions.cs`; keyword names are renamed (Q535). The ordinals are fixed.
